        <mxCell id="arrL2L3lbl" connectable="0" parent="arrL2L3" style="edgeLabel;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];fontSize=10;fillColor=#ffffff;" value="promoted facets&#xa;exposed via CQL2" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legendBox" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="1400" x="60" y="780" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legendTitle" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" value="Reading this diagram" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="24" width="500" x="76" y="786" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legendBody" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;fontSize=11;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;spacingLeft=8;" value="• L1 is hand-curated and lives in YAML. Each of the 11 entries carries a query_rule which Postgres materializes as a SQL view over L2.&lt;br&gt;• L2 is the harvested record - one row per ARC. Shared core (GeoJSON Feature + properties) is identical across domains; domain-specific fields live inside the assays[] sub-resources.&lt;br&gt;• L3 is not a separate document - it is a promotion contract. Selected L2 fields become CQL2 queryables (and OAI-PMH facets). Promotion is governed by an explicit rule (right column).&lt;br&gt;• A single ARC can satisfy several membership rules → it appears in multiple collections simultaneously (cross-membership is intrinsic).&lt;br&gt;• Controlled-vocabulary registry (vocabularies.yaml) is the single source of truth for enum value spaces referenced by both L2 schemas and the L3 queryable list." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="125" width="1380" x="76" y="810" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
